# Backend and sync
- Backend sync is optional; local storage is the default. Keep existing service boundaries: REST persists cloud state, WebSockets signal changes, and clients never connect to MongoDB directly.
- Sync and AI enablement are independent. Verify current opt-in flags before changes.
- `X-User-Id`, profile data, and socket `user_id` are not authentication. Don't expose sync publicly without verified auth, ownership/authorization, and tests.
- Validate payloads; never silently replace malformed remote dates with today. Don't log user content, credentials, tokens, or connection URIs.
- Check `backend/requirements.txt` before adding dependencies. Keep backend layout small; justify new technologies.
- `api_test.ps1` writes data and starts a server: use only an isolated test database, never personal/production data.
